[gd_scene format=3]

; WASH ASCENT — the ONE source of truth for level placements (director's
; consolidation ruling, 2026-07-28). Every visible object is a node here:
; either a Marker3D wearing metadata/piece (instantiated from the archetype
; piece library at its transform) or a real light. NOTHING is placed from
; code except the tiled fills that RUN markers declare (deck/wall/channel/
; rail/pipe runs advance along the marker's local +X, lengths measured from
; the pieces' real AABBs at load — never eyeballed).
;
; THE STORY (read the tree): a service walkway along a wash channel, built
; over years, decaying from the old end. The APPROACH is the oldest span —
; broken decking, a rail gap, scarpet in the damp seams, one flure calling
; to nobody. The MAINTENANCE BAY is the kept part — a worker's dwelling,
; bench, stores, the valve that works the channel. The MANIFOLD RUN feeds
; the water hardware — junction to junction, pipes mouth-to-mouth. The
; PORTAL LEDGE is the far end the overgrowth is taking back.

